{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Apply the 24-week abortion limit where Down syndrome is the sole ground",
        "additional_details": "We believe Down syndrome alone should not justify a different gestational limit. People with Down syndrome have equal worth, and we want the same time limit to apply where this condition alone is relied upon. Our proposal would preserve existing grounds protecting the pregnant woman\u2019s life and health, and other conditions that independently meet the legal criteria. Families also deserve accurate, balanced information and practical support.",
        "background": "Amend section 1(1)(d) of the Abortion Act 1967 in England and Wales so the 24-week limit applies where diagnosed or suspected Down syndrome is the sole basis for meeting that provision. Retain all other existing legal grounds for abortion.",
